= The Clegg Awards

During the Winter of Discontent, Labour set up Professor Clegg's commission to compare public-sector pay with the private sector. Its awards are now arriving, and they are expensive. During the campaign we promised to honour them.

- @honour: Honour the awards.
- @refuse: Refuse to pay in full.

@honour
on-arrival: budget -= 2; strike_wave -= 1; inflation += 0.5; wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 3

We keep our promise. Public-sector pay jumps, and so does public spending.

@refuse
on-arrival: strike_wave += 2; union_power += 3; thatcher_rating -= 2; c2_con -= 1; de_con -= 2; dry_dissent -= 3

We phase the awards and cut them back. The public-sector unions accuse us of breaking an election promise, and they have a point.
